Run 1 (HOME home, a person, Enter): the newest compiler that min-release-age allows is the download (the command names it, so Enter is yes); the default (a nightly) moves to it; the comments and the other keys of config.toml stay; the old compiler stays (R-RU4); the project in the current directory (a roc: pin) is not touched (R-RU3). Run 2: the newest is installed, so only the text `<id> is the newest`. Run 3 (`up`, `--offline`): the cached list answers. Run 4 (home2, CI): no prompt, the download starts (R-DL4); the default is a link build, so it stays and a note says how to change it. Run 5 (home3, CI, `--json`): the first compiler is the default (R-SO15), previous is null, changed is true. Run 6 (home4, TALON_NOW 2026-10-19): min-release-age hides the 2 newest nightlies (R-C7). Run 7 (home5, TALON_NIGHTLY=0): exit 10, the text names the switch (R-NS2). Run 8 (home6, `--offline`, no cached list): exit 15. Run 9: an operand is exit 2 with no Fx call. Run 10 (home7, a person, `n`): exit 13, nothing changes. Runs 11 to 13 (answer Q1 of the review, homes 8 to 10): the newest is installed already, nothing is downloaded, and the default still moves (older nightly, or not set: `installed` is false, `changed` is true) or stays with the note (a link build). Run 14 (answer Q2, home11): `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=no` does not refuse, because the command names the download (R-DL4).
